{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition","id":1013629,"title":"Rote Factors in 2nd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-07T01:00:33-08:00","id":1013629,"title":"Rote Factors in 2nd Edition","content":"I was thinking of adding Rote factors into 2e but applying it into Reach instead and here's what I've got:<br /> <br /> <b>Bound Rotes:</b> Bound Rotes are rotes that have incorporated certain symbolism to their Imago, making it easier for a Mage to reach beyond their ability if they use it's encoded Yantra. A Bound Rote's Yantra can be however difficult a Master wants them to be, indeed many Adamant Sages have used the Adamant Hand technique into their Rotes specifically so that it's power can only be fully used by their order.<br /> <br /> Systems: A Bound Rote has an optional effect which gives you free Reach but only to a certain option and if you use the Yantra that is required for the Reach. There is technically speaking no limits on how many Yantras 'bound' to a specific Rote but it requires 3 extra success make a Bound Rote, giving it a Yantra and it's associated Reach, and another 2 success to for each Yantra after that. This can only be done when the Rote is being created, a Rote cannot be turned into a Bound Rote even by the master who created it.<br /> <br /> Each Yantra used in the Rote can only 'give' 1 free Reach, an effect that requires 2 Reach must use two different but related yantras(Attacking a second leg after successfully hitting the other one for example) and anything that requires Mana must still be payed. Yantra's still give their associated bonus dice or effect(such as using Temporal Sympathy)<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:23:58-08:00","id":1013636,"title":"","content":"Looks good! I can see this being good for 3+ dot spells especially, where you burn up those free Reach from rotes fast.<br /> <br /> I like that it lets you create rotes that can only be learned by certain groups, like binding them to a Legacy oblation or Patron tool of a Seer or Scelestus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:52:30-08:00","id":1013651,"title":"","content":"I don't understand what this does, it looks like you're saying that Yantras grant Reach? That isn't how Yantras work though, they grant Dice. Is this supposed to give an even bigger Reach bonus than Rotes normally get (Being treated as a Master for that spell)? If so, how do you justify a Rote with more Reach than a Master can actually employ not being an automatic Paradox risk? It's also confusing because you say Rote factors in the title, but then you don't actually talk about factors at all. Are the required extra successes for creating the Rote or for casting it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:59:13-08:00","id":1013652,"title":"","content":"I think it works like in a 1e where you had extra feature in a rote but you needed to find in a grimuar or something. E.g. healing spell that gets free scale factor if you share a cup of wine with everybody you want to affect<br /> <br /> Edit: drinking from cup is a yantra that grants scale factor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T02:07:45-08:00","id":1013653,"title":"","content":"It feels like this needs some sort of drawback on the side of people learning the Rote in question. The extra successes needed to encode the Rote is reasonable, but fairly trivial for a Master to accomplish (They're probably going to have a dice-pool of 10, which means up to 10 rolls, and that's more than enough to stack on a lot of extra success for this unless the spell uses a number of different Arcana). Once they're made though... there's pretty much no downside to them.<br /> <br /> Why would you ever get a normal Rote instead of a Bound Rote if you have the chance? The Bound Rote gives you everything the normal Rote does, but you have the chance to get some free bonus Reach out of it if the conditions are right (and there's certain Reach options that are pretty much always going to be useful for a given spell).<br /> <br /> This also feels like it would make Masters+ obnoxiously powerful. They get to create their own Rotes to get five free Reach on master level spells... which seems like it's going to really not mesh well. A lot of the bonus Reach options at that level are aimed at either constraining using those options for ritual casting, or forcing overreach if you want to use them quickly. With these rules a master of Prime can make permanent Hallows in a few seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T02:24:39-08:00","id":1013656,"title":"","content":"I think it was introduced in Tome of Mysteries. Some kind of pre-alpha for reach mechanics. <br /> Anyway. It can offer specific reach option like 'travel a full scene' for a Shifting Sands if you wave a feather in the air. The drawback could be that the rote works only with that reach and yantra now.<br /> As far as I remember it was a story hook and a reward. If the cabal wanted to have such rote it needed to find it first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 12-07-2016, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T02:52:51-08:00","id":1013663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1013653#post1013653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like this needs some sort of drawback on the side of people learning the Rote in question. The extra successes needed to encode the Rote is reasonable, but fairly trivial for a Master to accomplish (They're probably going to have a dice-pool of 10, which means up to 10 rolls, and that's more than enough to stack on a lot of extra success for this unless the spell uses a number of different Arcana). Once they're made though... there's pretty much no downside to them.<br /> <br /> Why would you ever get a normal Rote instead of a Bound Rote if you have the chance? The Bound Rote gives you everything the normal Rote does, but you have the chance to get some free bonus Reach out of it if the conditions are right (and there's certain Reach options that are pretty much always going to be useful for a given spell).<br /> <br /> This also feels like it would make Masters+ obnoxiously powerful. They get to create their own Rotes to get five free Reach on master level spells... which seems like it's going to really not mesh well. A lot of the bonus Reach options at that level are aimed at either constraining using those options for ritual casting, or forcing overreach if you want to use them quickly. With these rules a master of Prime can make permanent Hallows in a few seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see this work if you use it as a modified Mudra. So instead of granting additional dice the Mudra only grants one reach. If you want to have the possibility to choose between both advantages, you have to learn two different rotes. This also limits the additional free reach to one, which is good, but not too game breaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T03:27:59-08:00","id":1013667,"title":"","content":"Would you still allow them to benefit from other Yantra dice-bonuses?<br /> <br /> I mean, having the trade off be dice or Reach works, and at start Rotes give some of the best dice bonuses, but as the game progresses it's more and more likely a character will be able to max out their bonuses without it and it reduces opportunity cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T03:42:36-08:00","id":1013671,"title":"","content":"Maybe we can treat it as different Yantra that you still need to incorporate and that takes time. One Yantra for Mudra and one Yantra that grants you a Reach effect (incantating a mambo jumbo about egyptian gods for Quicken Corpse).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T05:11:01-08:00","id":1013685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1013667#post1013667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you still allow them to benefit from other Yantra dice-bonuses?<br /> <br /> I mean, having the trade off be dice or Reach works, and at start Rotes give some of the best dice bonuses, but as the game progresses it's more and more likely a character will be able to max out their bonuses without it and it reduces opportunity cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I would allow other Yantras to work as usual. And I would let you buy that &quot;Reach Rote/Mudra&quot; for the same exp as a normal Rote. That way it comes with a price too, so that you can't just get additional reach with every Rote you already have. I would keep the benefits of the Rote (Reach like a Master) too. That way you could not use the standard Mudra and the &quot;Reach Mudra&quot; at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T05:37:29-08:00","id":1013701,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow any kind of Yantra to grant a Reach bonus, and I definitely wouldn't allow it to be something that Masters can do. If I were going to allow a larger than normal amount of free Reach on a Rote it would be because it's created by an archmaster. Maybe I'd restrict it from there, but probably by making it scarce rather than making it harder to enact via some mutilation of the Yantra rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:26:23-08:00","id":1013743,"title":"","content":"If you want a specific rituals that make specific ways to cast specific spells, create Conditions that resolve as a part of spellcasting and modify the spell in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:27:51-08:00","id":1013744,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in seeing an example of what you have in mind WHW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:39:15-08:00","id":1013751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1013701#post1013701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow any kind of Yantra to grant a Reach bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>But rotes already do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:12:18-08:00","id":1013771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1013744#post1013744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested in seeing an example of what you have in mind WHW</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Secret of Magical Cup<br /> Due to obtaining magical manual of Magical Cup and succeeding at investigating it's Mysteries, you obtained ability to incorporate it into your Magic. By [doing X, Y, Z] and succeeding at a check of XYZ, you may expend this Condition in order to [modify a spell in a specific way.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:19:37-08:00","id":1013774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1013751#post1013751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But rotes already do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they don't. Rotes generally grant a Reach bonus to someone who is not a Master, but they do not grant that bonus via Yantras.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you were agreeing with my stance by pointing out that it is in fact the way Rotes work that they don't grant Reach via Yantras. In which case my response is: I know. I'm stating that any houserules I made that did grant bonus Reach beyond the norm would be inline with that guideline of not providing it via Yantras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:20:56-08:00","id":1013777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1013771#post1013771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Secret of Magical Cup<br /> Due to obtaining magical manual of Magical Cup and succeeding at investigating it's Mysteries, you obtained ability to incorporate it into your Magic. By [doing X, Y, Z] and succeeding at a check of XYZ, you may expend this Condition in order to [modify a spell in a specific way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I still don't get it. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T11:20:42-08:00","id":1013857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1013777#post1013777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I still don't get it. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1013652#post1013652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it works like in a 1e where you had extra feature in a rote but you needed to find in a grimuar or something. E.g. healing spell that gets free scale factor if you share a cup of wine with everybody you want to affect</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Condition - Secret of Magical Cup</u><br /> Your character has learned the secret of the magical cup. When casting a spell that heals or downgrades wounds, you may expend this Condition to increase the spell's Scale Factor to Advanced without spending a Reach. However, the spell can only affect subjects who have shared a cup of wine with you since you acquired this Condition. Expending the Condition in this way does not count as resolving it, and does not grant a Beat.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your knowledge of the magical cup is erased or stolen by magic.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Successful completion of the Quest for the Magical Cup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T11:40:06-08:00","id":1013871,"title":"","content":"Ok, that's pretty cool. Thanks Charlaquin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:02:42-08:00","id":1013929,"title":"","content":"Pretty much that, though I would make obtaining the Condition reliant on preparing the &quot;rote factor&quot; to work and not making the Condition itself permanent. <br /> <br /> So basically:<br /> <br /> 1. You need to own knowledge of Magical Cup. This can be a Merit, a book, or other similar resource.<br /> 2. This thing specifies a priming condition. For example, the Cup might require sanctifying the Cup in a specific way that should non-trivial enough so you can't really expect the Mage to keep spamming it. <br /> 3. Doing that thing - for example, preparing the Cup - rewards you with the Condition.<br /> 4. Condition explains how the &quot;spell secret&quot; works, and is expanded after being used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T03:25:48-08:00","id":1014232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1013701#post1013701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow any kind of Yantra to grant a Reach bonus, and I definitely wouldn't allow it to be something that Masters can do. If I were going to allow a larger than normal amount of free Reach on a Rote it would be because it's created by an archmaster. Maybe I'd restrict it from there, but probably by making it scarce rather than making it harder to enact via some mutilation of the Yantra rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't allow that in my game either, but if you want to have rotes granting Reach, the way I discribed is what I would mechanically aim for.<br /> <br /> Like that condition thing, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T03:31:49-08:00","id":1014233,"title":"","content":"I won't be suprised if you find something like that in Signs of Sorcery. It's a cool story hook for an advanture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T04:41:26-08:00","id":1014246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1014232#post1014232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't allow that in my game either, but if you want to have rotes granting Reach, the way I discribed is what I would mechanically aim for.<br /> <br /> Like that condition thing, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mudra is a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T06:52:16-08:00","id":1014289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1013629-rote-factors-in-2nd-edition?p=1014246#post1014246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Mudra is a Yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of this and I don't really understand what you want to tell me with the comment, but I try to elaborate:<br /> <br /> The OP asked for a way to introduce free reach through rotes. I gave a suggestion doing this by adding an additional kind of Rote, where the Mudra does not give you additional dice, but a free Reach. Since you cannot use two Mudras in one spell, you have to chose if you get the free Reach or the dice bonus.<br /> <br /> While I think this an okay way to get one additional free Reach via special Rotes without totally breaking the system, I would personally not use this for my own games, since I think the system works well the way it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T10:25:53-08:00","id":1014366,"title":"","content":"You had just quoted me saying that I wouldn't allow Yantras to grant Reach, agreed with me, and then said you would allow the Mudra Yantra to grant Reach. So I pointed out that your position actually seems to be in conflict with mine because a Mudra is a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T14:11:24-08:00","id":1014450,"title":"","content":"He doesn't think it's a good idea, but he is proposing a solution to someone who *does* think that it is a good idea. He is basically suggesting that when casting a spell, you choose between two mutually exclusive Mudra options - one that grants Dice Bonuses, and one that grants Reach. You can't combine them, because they are both Mudras, and you can only include one Mudra in the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T17:06:21-08:00","id":1014523,"title":"","content":"I know what their suggestion was. I'm also not confused. I was clarifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}